    "388": {
      "date": "2026-10-14",
      "edition": "Wednesday 14 October",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Obituary",
          "heading": "Fergus Slattery, Ireland's 61-cap flanker and 1974 Lion, died aged 77",
          "body": "The Telegraph's obituary, published 4 June, marks the death of Fergus Slattery, who was 77. Slattery won 61 caps for Ireland between 1970 and 1984, including 18 as captain, and led the 1979 tour of Australia. He was also in the 1974 British and Irish Lions back row in South Africa, alongside England's Roger Uttley and Wales's Mervyn Davies, a trio the obituary says many still regard as the best Lions back row combination ever. At his retirement his 61 caps were a world record for a flanker."
        },
        {
