          "kicker": "Legal action",
          "heading": "World Rugby loses bid to have brain injury claims thrown out",
          "body": "World Rugby and UK governing bodies lost their bid to have brain injury claims brought by rugby players thrown out of court, a ruling reported on 21 August. Later reports say hundreds of players have won the right for their claims to go to trial. The Guardian reports the claimants now face a £2.8m legal bill to keep the case going, and the case remains open. Italy are not named in any of the coverage I have seen, so the Azzurri's stake is indirect."
        },
