    "461": {
      "date": "2026-10-14",
      "edition": "Wednesday 14 October",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Selection blow",
          "heading": "Len Ikitau, Hunter Paisami, Jordan Petaia out; Suaalii may return to centre",
          "body": "Len Ikitau (concussion), Hunter Paisami (suspension) and Jordan Petaia (ankle) are all ruled out of Saturday's second Bledisloe Cup Test against New Zealand, and Joseph-Aukuso Suaalii could move back into the centres after two games on the wing. Suaalii, who played 24 successive Tests at outside centre before the switch, says he is enjoying the change, telling reporters in Sydney that it is 'a different part of my journey.' The match is at Accor Stadium, where Australia will try to bounce back from the 50-19 Eden Park defeat."
        }
      ],
      "match": {
        "venue": "Accor Stadium, Sydney"
      },
      "source": {
        "name": "Planet Rugby"
      }
    },
    "463": {
      "date": "2026-10-14",
      "edition": "Wednesday 14 October",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Sevens success",
          "heading": "Japan Sakura Sevens reclaim Asian Games women's gold; men take bronze",
          "body": "The Japan Sakura Sevens reclaimed Asian Games women's gold in Aichi-Nagoya, beating defending champions China 10-5 in a tight final, as reported on 5 October. Japan's men took bronze after a 17-5 win over Korea, having lost a semi-final 10-7 to China, a result seen as an upset. Hong Kong China completed a three-peat of men's titles, winning the final 26-0."
        },
